  "id": "Compound::DB00209 - Gene::1129",
  "verbalization": "Trospium, a drug, is shown to bind to Chrm1, a receptor involved in the activation of G-protein coupled acetylcholine or neurotransmitter receptors. This binding leads to the participation of Chrm1 in activities that are broadly associated with muscarinic and nicotinic receptor functions. The evidence suggests that Trospium may influence Chrm2 through a mechanism involving the activation of G-protein coupled receptors, as Chrm2 is part of the receptor family that is targeted by these activities. The overlapping pathways across the three paths indicate a potential role for Trospium in modulating Chrm2 through receptor activation, possibly by enhancing the function of G-protein coupled receptors in the cell. The integration of these pathways highlights a possible mechanism by which Trospium could interact with Chrm2, though the exact nature of the interaction remains to be fully elucidated.",
